  <constraints>
    <constraint source="DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE §3 / CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: the rule. The reconciler decides each child's owner ONLY by calling `IRecordOwnershipResolver` with the same inputs task 146's writers pass, and applies shares ONLY through task 149's reconcile(root). No second implementation of either rule — not in the job, not in a PowerShell script. A script, if any, only triggers or reports.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: transition ordering. PROVISIONING: root isolated (Step 5) → root shared (Step 5.5) → child shares mirrored (task 149 mechanism) → children re-owned → reconcile(root) verifies → (container steps unchanged). Mirroring BEFORE the re-own is deliberate: POA shares survive an Assign, so sharees never lose a child mid-pass — task 149 Part A must confirm that shares survive Assign; if it shows they do not, the order becomes re-own → mirror and the transient under-share (never an over-share) is recorded in the note. UNSECURE: root re-owned (Step 3) → children re-owned to their non-secure owner → child mirrored shares removed → root shares revoked (Step 4) → flag cleared last (Step 5). INVARIANT at every moment of either transition: no child is readable by a principal who is not entitled to it (no over-share, ever); a former secure child is never reachable by nobody at the END of an unsecure pass; a partially complete pass fails toward under-share and reports it (ADR-003).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every transition response. A child pass that does not complete is NOT reported as success: the response carries a stable reason code and a message with per-table counts of children re-owned / remaining, not a bare 500. Unsecure with a failed child pass does NOT clear `sprk_issecure` (the flag keeps meaning "children may still be isolated"). The root steps already committed are not rolled back.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: resumability. Every operation is idempotent (a child already in its target state is skipped and counted); re-invoking provisioning or unsecure on a root whose child pass is incomplete completes the pass instead of returning 409/200-no-op, and the sweep job completes it regardless. Coordinate with task 133 (C11 — creator lock-out / resumable provisioning on the same endpoint) — do not implement two resume paths.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036 / ADR-052">Scope: the sweep. It is an `IScheduledJob` in the BFF (no hand-rolled BackgroundService), registered DISABLED with writes REPORT-ONLY by default (the ExternalAccessReconciliationJob posture), running every `sprk_issecure = true` root of all three types, ordered by root id, with a per-run cap and a progress log so an interrupted run resumes. Placement decision recorded per ADR-052.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: every assign. Owner changes are separate assign operations verified by read-back (`ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:597-616` rationale), never folded into a field PATCH. Each changed row's previous owner is recorded in the run report before the write (reversal evidence).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2">Scope: data. Unfiled documents (no parent) are never touched. Do not relax the alternate key on the SPE item id. A failed revoke returns a message, not a bare 500.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-1 / ADR-002">Scope: all of it. No Dataverse plugin. Live verification is a MANUAL gate (no Dataverse in CI); existing non-admin test users in their current BU; never propose relocating users. Probe records are deleted afterwards and the deletion recorded.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration or ctor null-check tests. Transition tests under `tests/integration/data-mutation/**` using the existing provisioning fixtures.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement decision citing bff-extensions.md and ADR-052; publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (short path, Compress-Archive, both sizes, file counts), ≤60 MB; CVE scan.</constraint>
  </constraints>

